{'symbol': 'WFC', 'date': '2020-02-22 20:30:00', 'title': 'Wells Fargo Reaches Settlements To Resolve Outstanding DOJ And SEC Investigations Over Sales Practices', 'text': 'WELLS FARGO REACHES SETTLEMENTS TO RESOLVE OUTSTANDING DOJ AND SEC INVESTIGATIONS RELATED TO HISTORICAL COMMUNITY BANK SALES PRACTICES.WELLS FARGO & CO - AS PART OF THIS RESOLUTION, WELLS FARGO HAS AGREED TO MAKE PAYMENTS TOTALING $3 BILLION..WELLS FARGO & CO - SETTLEMENT INCLUDES AGREEMENT WITH DOJ RESOLVING CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION.WELLS FARGO & CO - RESOLUTION ALSO COVERS DOJ AND SEC CIVIL INVESTIGATIONS.WELLS FARGO & CO - AS PART OF AGREEMENT, NO CHARGES WILL BE FILED AGAINST WELLS FARGO PROVIDED WELLS FARGO ABIDES BY ALL TERMS OF AGREEMENT.WELLS FARGO & CO - HAD FULLY ACCRUED FOR AMOUNT OF SETTLEMENT AS OF DECEMBER 31, 2019.WELLS FARGO & CO - UNDER RESOLUTION CO AGREED TO ESTABLISHMENT OF $500 MILLION FAIR FUND FOR BENEFIT OF INVESTORS HARMED BY CONDUCT COVERED IN AGREEMENT.WELLS FARGO & CO - $500 MILLION FAIR FUND IS PART OF $3 BILLION SETTLEMENT.WELLS FARGO- AGREEMENT WITH DOJ RESOLVES CRIMINAL INVESTIGATION INTO SALES PRACTICE ACTIVITIES IN COMMUNITY BANK FROM 2002 - 2016.'}
